;; min-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `min-fencei.s` (P2-SCALAR.6).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py min-fencei.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "min-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `min-fencei.s`." "" "⛔ THE RETAINED MINIMIZED CASE (P2-SCALAR.6): one word reproduces DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED — semulith's" "policy trap lands at step 0 (the divergence IS the first step; the prefix agreement is vacuous)." "Both references nop the fence.i and run off the end into the zero word — illegal-instruction on" "each, measured (P2-SCALAR.4; run_probes_p25s3.py) — so they stay each other's control over their" "full 2-step length. Nothing was widened or edited to close anything (EVD-05, AI-05): the" "divergence stands, minimized and retained.")
(expectations (program "min-fencei.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 1) (expect_divergence (difference "DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED") (at_step 0)) (step (n 0) (insn ".word 0x0000100F") (writes) (derivation "0x0000100F is fence.i. Zifencei is absent from this profile, so the word matches no row of the generated decode table: a RESERVED instruction, whose behavior the architecture declares UNSPECIFIED. The laboratory's policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) raises illegal-instruction with tval = the offending word: cause 0x02, tval 0x000000000000100F — and the run stops (Stop::Undefined keeps the source classification, SEM-07). Both references instead nop it (measured) — the legitimate UNSPECIFIED divergence, minimized to its first step.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (the reserved-instruction note: UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE; DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED (references.sexp)")))
